<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_volunteers" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Volunteer Coordination</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html">
            <p>Setting up roles and shifts, running the day, screening
            volunteers, and reporting hours.</p>
        </field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('event.group_event_user')])]" />
    </record>

    <!-- ================= Section 1: Roles and shifts ================= -->
    <record id="section_roles" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Roles and shifts</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_roles_shifts" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Adding roles to an event, and running one as shifts</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>Open the event and go to its <strong>Volunteers</strong>
                tab. Add a role - a name ("Setup Crew", "Greeter", "Net
                Control"), how many people it needs, and a short description
                volunteers will see on the website.</p>

                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <div class="oe-columns">
                        <div class="oe-column">
                            <h4><i class="fa fa-square-o" /> Whole-event role</h4>
                            <p class="mb-0 text-muted">One block covering the
                            entire event.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="oe-column">
                            <h4><i class="fa fa-clock-o" /> Run as Shifts</h4>
                            <p class="mb-0">Tick <strong>Run as
                            Shifts</strong>, then add shifts - each a time
                            window and a slot count.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Illustration</span>
                        the two ways a role can be filled.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-calendar" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Seeing it all at once</span>
                        <p>The <strong>Shifts</strong> stat button on the
                        event shows every shift on a calendar.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_recurring" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Recurring shifts for a weekly program</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>On an <strong>Event Type</strong> (Events ›
                Configuration › Event Types), add Recurring Volunteer
                Shift lines: role name, weekday, start time, length, slots.
                Give your recurring event that type.</p>

                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <div class="oe-flow">
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-list" /></span>
                            Event Type shift lines
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-moon-o" /></span>
                            Nightly job
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-calendar-check-o" /></span>
                            Shifts on the calendar
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Illustration</span>
                        a nightly job creates shifts as far ahead as the
                        horizon in settings, without duplicating ones it's
                        already made.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-good">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-bolt" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Need them sooner?</span>
                        <p>Open the event and click <strong>Generate shifts
                        from event type</strong>.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ===================== Section 2: On the day ===================== -->
    <record id="section_day" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">On the day</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_checkin" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Check-in, check-out, and no-shows</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <div class="oe-flow">
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-sign-in" /></span>
                            Check In
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-sign-out" /></span>
                            Check Out
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-clock-o" /></span>
                            Hours calculated automatically
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Illustration</span>
                        front desk clicks these as each volunteer arrives and
                        leaves.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-warn">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-user-times" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Didn't show up?</span>
                        <p>Click <strong>No-show</strong> on their assignment:
                        it's kept for the record but left out of hours
                        reports.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_swaps" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Shift swaps</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <div class="oe-diagram">
                    <div class="oe-flow">
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-user" /></span>
                            Volunteer offers shift
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-user-plus" /></span>
                            Another volunteer claims it
                        </div>
                        <span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span>
                        <div class="oe-flow-step">
                            <span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-check-square-o" /></span>
                            Coordinator approves
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="oe-diagram-caption">
                        <span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Illustration</span>
                        approval, under <strong>Events › Shift
                        Swaps</strong>, is what actually reassigns the
                        shift.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-warn">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-shield" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Screening still applies</span>
                        <p>The volunteer taking it still has to meet whatever
                        screening the role requires.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================== Section 3: Screening =================== -->
    <record id="section_screening" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Screening volunteers</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_screening_records" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Skills, background checks &amp; waivers</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">31</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>All set up on the volunteer's own contact record, under
                the <strong>Volunteer</strong> tab. Tag
                <strong>Skills</strong> (First Aid, Spanish, Licensed
                Driver…) from the list under Events › Configuration
                › Volunteer Skills.</p>

                <div class="oe-columns">
                    <div class="oe-column">
                        <h4><i class="fa fa-id-card" /> Background check</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">Set it to Requested when you start
                        one, and click <strong>Mark Cleared</strong> once it
                        comes back - that stamps today's date and sets the
                        re-check due date from the validity in settings.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="oe-column">
                        <h4><i class="fa fa-file-text" /> Liability waiver</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">Print it from the contact's Print
                        menu (it adapts for minors), collect the signed copy,
                        then click <strong>Record Waiver Accepted</strong> to
                        stamp the date.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-good">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-bell" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Nothing to watch by hand</span>
                        <p>A nightly job flips lapsed checks to Expired and
                        raises a to-do for the Volunteer Coordinator ahead of
                        expiry, so nobody has to watch a calendar.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-child" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">A minor volunteer</span>
                        <p>Tick <strong>Under 18</strong> and record the
                        parent/guardian - the waiver PDF picks them up
                        automatically.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_require_it" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Making a role require it</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">32</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <p>On the volunteer role, tick <strong>Requires Background
                Check</strong> and/or <strong>Requires Waiver</strong>, and
                add any <strong>Required Skills</strong>.</p>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-warn">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-ban" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">The gate is enforced everywhere</span>
                        <p>From then on, a sign-up - on the website or in the
                        back office - from a volunteer who isn't cleared,
                        hasn't a current waiver, or lacks a skill is refused,
                        with a message saying exactly what's missing.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout oe-callout-good">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-magic" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Looking for the right person instead?</span>
                        <p>Click <strong>Suggest Volunteers</strong> on a
                        shift to get everyone who has every required skill,
                        is cleared and waivered as the role needs, and isn't
                        already booked on an overlapping shift.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================== Section 4: Reporting ==================== -->
    <record id="section_reporting" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Reporting</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">40</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_hours" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Volunteer hours and certificates</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">41</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <div class="oe-course-content">
                <div class="oe-columns">
                    <div class="oe-column">
                        <h4><i class="fa fa-table" /> Volunteer Hours</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">A pivot by volunteer, program, event,
                        or month.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="oe-column">
                        <h4><i class="fa fa-certificate" /> Hours Certificates</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">A per-volunteer PDF for a chosen year,
                        listing every shift and the total - handy for
                        students and court-ordered service.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="oe-callout">
                    <span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-exclamation-circle" /></span>
                    <div>
                        <span class="oe-callout-label">Understaffed Shifts</span>
                        <p>Lists upcoming shifts still short of people, all
                        under <strong>Events › Volunteer
                        Reporting</strong>.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ========================= Quiz ========================= -->
    <record id="slide_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_volunteers" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="slide_category">quiz</field>
        <field name="sequence">90</field>
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q1" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="question">A role needs a background check. What happens if an uncleared volunteer tries to sign up?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">The sign-up is refused, with a message saying what's missing</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed, with a warning email sent later</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed only from the back office, not the website</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's allowed, since background checks are informational only</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q2" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="question">Who gets notified before a volunteer's background check expires?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">The Volunteer Coordinator, via an automatic to-do</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">Nobody - you have to check manually</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">The volunteer only, by text message</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">The front desk, at check-in</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q3" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="question">How do recurring weekly shifts get created?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">You add each one by hand every week</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">A nightly job builds them from Recurring Volunteer Shift lines on the event type</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Volunteers create their own shifts</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">They copy from last year's event automatically with no setup</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q4" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="question">A volunteer didn't show up for their shift. What do you click?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Delete their assignment</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">No-show</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Check In, then Check Out immediately</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Offer the shift for swap on their behalf</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

</odoo>
